############################################################################
#
# TEMPLATE for scripts/<system>/profile.local.sh.
#
# Copy to scripts/<system>/profile.local.sh (e.g. scripts/tuolumne/) and edit.
# That path is gitignored, which is the whole point: this file records facts
# about ONE CHECKOUT on ONE MACHINE, and committing it would impose your
# checkout's choices on every clone.
#
#   Per-instance (here)         build mode; which env this checkout is developed
#                               into; the build directory.
#   Per-system (committed)      scripts/<system>/profile.defaults.sh — fallbacks
#                               so a fresh clone works with zero configuration,
#                               plus runtime_env.sh for launch-time exports.
#   Project-wide (committed)    CLAUDE.md, tests/CMakeLists.txt.
#
# Only set what DIFFERS from that system's profile.defaults.sh. Anything you
# leave out falls through to the fallback, so a short file is a good file.
#
# Use ${VAR:=value}, not VAR=value: the resolver visits environment, then this
# file, then the defaults, and `:=` makes the first assignment win. A plain
# `VAR=value` here would stomp an explicit environment override on the command
# line, breaking `BEATNIK_USE_PROD=1 flux batch ...` and similar.
############################################################################

# --- Build mode: "spack" or "manual" -------------------------------------
#
# spack   The environment provides dependencies AND builds Beatnik
#         (`spack develop` + `spack install`); binaries land on PATH; there is
#         no build tree, so the gate runs installed binaries via the scheduler.
#         In this mode NEVER hand-run cmake/make.
#
# manual  The environment provides dependencies only; you compile out-of-tree
#         into BEATNIK_BUILD_DIR and the gate is ctest in that directory.
#         In this mode `spack install` is NOT the build command.
#
# Do not mix the two in one checkout.
: "${BEATNIK_BUILD_MODE:=spack}"

# --- Environments this checkout targets ----------------------------------
# Override only if this checkout is developed into something other than the
# machine default. Keep the path absolute or ${HOME}-relative.
#: "${BEATNIK_SPACK_ENV:=${HOME}/spack_envs/my_beatnik_dev}"
#: "${BEATNIK_SPACK_PROD_ENV:=${HOME}/spack_envs/my_beatnik_prod}"

# --- Build directory (manual mode only) ----------------------------------
# Defaults to ${BEATNIK_REPO}/build-<system>, which is already unique per
# clone. Override only to move it off a slow or small filesystem.
#: "${BEATNIK_BUILD_DIR:=/p/lustre5/${USER}/beatnik-build}"

# --- Notes for whoever picks up this checkout ----------------------------
# Free-form. Since this file is not committed, it is the right place for
# anything true of this checkout alone — which branch it tracks, which
# experiment it is pinned to, why it deviates from the machine default.
#
# e.g. "spack develop'd into tuolumne_beatnik; do not hand-build."
